  "description_html": "Size comparison of two species of the Chinese thalattosaur <i>Xinpusaurus</i>. The size of each species is based on their holotype specimen. The diver silhoutte is from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scuba33.jpg\" title=\"File:Scuba33.jpg\">File:Scuba33.jpg</a>, which is by NOAA and in the public domain.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Liu, Jun (2013). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://lveho.ivpp.cas.cn/kycg/lw/201404/P020140409561017065607.pdf\">On the taxonomy of <i>Xinpusaurus</i> (Reptilia:Thalattosauria)</a>\". <i>Vertebrata Palasiatica</i> <b>51</b> (1): 17-23.</cite></li>\n<li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Jiang, Da-Yong; Motani, Ryosuke; Tintori, Andrea; Rieppel, Olivier; Ji, Cheng; Zhou, Min; Wang, Xue; Lu, Hao; Li, Zhi-Guang (2020). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2589004220305344%7Cjournal=iScience\">Evidence supporting predation of 4-m marine reptile by Triassic megapredator</a>\". <i>iScience</i> <b>23</b> (9): 101347.</cite></li></ul>",
